Material3UI Shell v2 is a modified version of NAnDoroid-shell
(https://github.com/na-ive/nandoroid-shell, upstream commit
73d8892d571818944d09fbbca427fc0098b6a6f4), Copyright (C) na-ive and
NAnDoroid-shell contributors. NAnDoroid-shell is licensed under the GNU Affero
General Public License v3.0; its authors have permitted the code used here to
be relicensed under the MIT License for Material3UI Shell.

Modifications include: rebranding to Material3UI (Quickshell profile, config,
cache and Hyprland module paths), a unified "material3ui" IPC target, the
bundled material3uictl CLI, an original logo replacing the NAnDoroid artwork, wallpaper IPC functions, a Material3UI v1 migration
path in the installer, and the Midnight Dunes wallpaper.

From v4 the Quickshell (QML) shell is removed and replaced by the native C++
shell in shell/. Parts of the repository that came from NAnDoroid-shell and
remain (the Matugen templates and theme hooks, and the Hyprland configuration
layout) keep the attribution above.

Material3UI Shell is distributed under the MIT License, WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
see the LICENSE file for details.

The native C++ shell in shell/ follows the architecture of Noctalia
(https://github.com/noctalia-dev/noctalia, MIT). It is an independent implementation;
no Noctalia source code is included.

shell/data/icons/hyprland-logo.svg is the Hyprland logo, cropped to its drop from
assets/header.svg in Hyprland (https://github.com/hyprwm/Hyprland), Copyright (c)
Hyprland contributors, under the BSD-3-Clause license. It is used only to name
Hyprland in Settings → About and on the login screen, and does not imply
endorsement.

shell/data/icons/niri-logo.svg is the niri icon, docs/wiki/logo/niri-icon.svg in
niri (https://github.com/niri-wm/niri), by the niri contributors, licensed under
CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). It is recoloured
here from red and orange to teal (the logo is meant to be recoloured) and cropped
to its artwork, and that file stays under CC BY-SA 4.0. It is used only to name
niri in Settings → About and on the login screen, and does not imply endorsement.

shell/data/maps/world.svg, the time zone map in Settings → System, is drawn from
Natural Earth's 1:50m land, lakes and country borders
(https://www.naturalearthdata.com), which are in the public domain;
scripts/generate_world_map.py makes it.
